<!-- COMPILED STYLESHEET, not a runtime one. Built with the Tailwind CLI from the
     former inline theme config plus the hand-written component CSS, then inlined:
     this is a one-page app, so a separate file would only add a render-blocking
     round trip.

     Consequence: a Tailwind utility class that does not already appear somewhere in
     this file WILL NOT WORK until the stylesheet is rebuilt. Editing existing classes,
     or writing plain CSS into this block, needs no rebuild.

     Layer order below is deliberate. Component rules (.field, .chip, .seg) sit in the
